{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return rules","requirement":"A lessor may not require a security deposit above the first month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay five per cent yearly interest, and return the deposit with an itemized list of deductions within thirty days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent (deposit cap); 5% interest per year; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Rentals of residential real property in Massachusetts; the section sets no building age, size or owner limits.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Deposit-transfer liability does not apply to a city or town taking title under chapter 60 or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution; a landlord may still recover a deposit for wilful or malicious damage exceeding it.","penalty":"On violations of the account, transfer or return rules the tenant is awarded three times the deposit or balance plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees; failure to pay interest owed carries three times that interest.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2);","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts limit on upfront amounts a lessor may charge","requirement":"At or before the start of a tenancy a lessor or its agent may not require payment beyond first month's rent, last month's rent, a security deposit equal to one month's rent, and the cost of a key and lock.","key_value":"first month's rent + last month's rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key/lock cost","coverage_conditions":"Any residential tenancy; the cap binds a lessor or the lessor's agent and applies before or at the commencement of the tenancy.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"An executive-office regulation may authorize an optional fee in lieu of a security deposit, capped in total at 1 month's rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following: (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and, (iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts deposit-alternative fee must be offered without regard to income or credit","requirement":"A lessor that offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit must offer it to every applicant whose application is approved, regardless of income, credit score and other listed characteristics, and may not use those factors to set the fee amount.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies only if the executive office of housing and livable communities promulgates regulations authorizing a fee in lieu of a security deposit, and to lessors who offer such a fee.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"a lessor who offers a fee in lieu of a security deposit to an approved applicant","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(E) require a lessor who offers such a fee in lieu of security deposit:  (I) to offer the option of a fee in lieu of a security deposit to every prospective tenant whose application for occupancy has been approved, regardless of income, race, gender, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, immigration status, size of household or credit score;  and (II) not to consider such factors and categories when setting the amount of the fee;","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.6,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
